    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d210-a1">

                <pb facs="0315" n="241" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg241"/>

                <head>Mr. Hendricks to Mr. Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Senate Chamber</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington City,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-06-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 28, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> The Rev. John McMahon, the parish priest of
                    Anderson, in the State of Indiana, was recently called to visit Canada on
                    business connected with the estate of a deceased brother, and whilst there was
                    arrested and lodged in the jail at Toronto, upon the charge of being connected
                    with the Fenian invasion of that country, and he is now in the jail. I am
                    satisfied by the information which I have that he was not in Canada upon any
                    connection with the Fenian movement, but only upon proper business. I have the
                    honor, therefore, to request that you will use the influence of your department
                    with the authorities of Canada for the release of the reverend gentleman.</p>
                <p>With great respect,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOMAS A. HENDRICKS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
